{title: 161 - Throned Upon the Awful Tree}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #161 • ARFON • 7.7.7.8.7.7}
{lyricist: John Ellerton}
{composer: Traditional melody}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 161}
{meta: tune ARFON}
{meta: meter 7.7.7.8.7.7}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]Throned upon [Gm]the awful [Dm]tree,
[Gm]Lamb [Gbm]of [Gm]God, [Adim]Your [Gm]grief [Gbm]we [Gm]see.
[Gm]Darkness veils Your anguished face;
[Bb]None its [Adim]lines of [Gm/D]woe can [Bb]trace.
[Cm]None can [Gm/D]tell [Dm]what [Bb]pangs unknown
[Cm/G]Hold You [Gm]silent and alone.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]Silent [Gm]through those three [Dm]dread hours,
[Gm]Wrestling [Gbm]with [Gm]the [Adim]evil [Gbm]powers,
[Gm]Left alone with human sin,
[Bb]Gloom around [Adim]You and [Gm/D]within,
[Cm]Till th'appointed [Bb]time is nigh,
[Cm/G]Till the [Gm]Lamb of God may [Gbm]die.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm]Hark, that [Gm]cry that peals [Dm]aloud
[Gm]Upward through [Adim]the [Gm]whelming cloud!
[Gm]You, the Father's only Son,
[Bb]You, His [Adim]own anointed [Bb]one,
[Cm]You are [Gm/D]asking- [Bb]can it be?
[Cm/G]"Why have [Gm]You forsaken [Gbm]Me?"
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Dm]Lord, should [Gm]fear and anguish [Dm]roll
[Gm]Darkly o'er [Adim]our [Gm]sinful soul,
[Gm]You, who once were thus bereft
[Bb]That Your [Adim]own might ne'er [Gm/D]be [Bb]left,
[Cm]Teach us [Gm/D]by [Dm]that [Bb]bitter cry
[Cm/G]In the [Gm]gloom to know You [Gbm]nigh.
{end_of_verse}
